    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "302f2713_22bcde68",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/ShaderModule.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-26T06:12:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would like to use `ShaderModuleParseResult` for shader module creation in the same way for both cache missed (it will be generated by `ParseShaderModule`) and cache hit (it will be loaded from blob cache). If loaded from blob cache, the `uncacheableParseResult` is `nullopt` and `cacheableParseResult` holds value, while if generated by `ParseShaderModule`, the `uncacheableParseResult` holds value and `cacheableParseResult` could be `nullopt` if not needed (e.g. for Tint program regeneration).\n\nComments added in `ShaderModule.h` to make it clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "2d521364_f070e87e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
